From cfa62b88fb84f05dd866eb08775e6657c9045f48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:48:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] test(2d): pin the pecked tab window dives of contour-tabs

PR #3866 (#3678) pecks the three later tab window dives of the
contour-tabs catalog case, so the #3679 verifier names no dive and the
old expectation of three 6 mm findings failed on main.

The pin now asserts no PlungeTooDeep finding and that each dive column
on the last level steps Z 4, 2, 0, at most one 2 mm stepdown at a time.
A second test keeps the law pinned end to end: the same case with its
top 4 mm under the stock top names its four 4 mm dives, advisory only.

Fixes #3925

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
